<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>WinExe</OutputType>
    <!-- Windows 10.0.19041 target gives us the built-in Windows.Media.Ocr engine (free, on-device) -->
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFramework>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion>10.0.19041.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <ApplicationManifest>app.manifest</ApplicationManifest>
    <AssemblyName>PWRUHelper</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>PWRUHelper</RootNamespace>
    <Version>0.16.0</Version>
    <ApplicationIcon>assets\icon.ico</ApplicationIcon>
    <!-- The test project lives under tests\ inside this folder; keep its sources out of the
         app's default .cs/.xaml globbing (it has its own csproj). -->
    <DefaultItemExcludes>$(DefaultItemExcludes);tests\**</DefaultItemExcludes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- window / taskbar icon -->
    <Resource Include="assets\icon.png" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Let the test project reach the internal surface: pure helpers (ChunkText, version parsing),
         the policy and gate types, and since E4.S1 TranslationCacheStore plus CachingTranslator's
         store-taking constructor (internal so TranslationPolicyTests' GetConstructors().Single() holds) -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="PWRUHelper.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Used for capturing the selected screen region (GDI CopyFromScreen) -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" Version="8.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- E8.S2 / ruling E8-d — the ONE new NuGet this design allows, and it is on the PROTOTYPE
         BRANCH only (NFR6, architecture-cible.md §7.6). The MANAGED BINDING AND NOTHING ELSE:
         `ExcludeAssets="native"` keeps the 21.4 MB `bergamot.dll` out of the build output and out
         of the single-file bundle, which is U7's whole answer — E8.S1 measured 0 B of exe growth
         and `%TEMP%\.net\PWRUHelper\<id>` still at its five WPF files, so §7.6 constraint 4's
         self-extraction worry (the mechanism implicated in P1) is NOT re-armed.

         Read that 0 B for what it measured: E8.S1 held this package on the TEST csproj, where the
         app exe could not grow whatever happened. What the spike proved is the NATIVE half — the
         21.4 MB stays out and `%TEMP%\.net` does not re-arm — and that half carries over verbatim,
         confirmed here: no `runtimes/` directory in any build output and no `runtimeTargets` entry
         in `PWRUHelper.deps.json`. The MANAGED binding does now enter the bundle, deliberately (the
         production seam does not compile without it) and measurably: 9,728 B. That is the whole
         cost, against 21.4 MB avoided. `PrivateAssets` is NOT set on purpose — it would stop the
         assembly flowing to the test project, where the build-output pin reads it. The DLL is
         downloaded beside the models by E8.S3's store and reached through
         NativeLibrary.SetDllImportResolver (Services/BergamotEngine.cs). `PublishFlagsTests` is
         untouched by design (CI-7): this changes no publish flag in any of the three build paths.

         LICENCE OBLIGATION (§7.6 constraint 8, NFR10). The binding, the native engine and the
         models are all MPL-2.0 while this app is MIT. File-level copyleft is compatible with
         shipping beside an MIT app — and SignPath Foundation's requirement that the app itself
         stay OSI-licensed (MIT) is met — but it is a SECOND LICENCE and it has to be visible: the
         MPL text ships with the downloaded artefacts, and the About tab carries the notice. The
         placement of that block is E8.S3's (§4.2's "Offline engine (optional)") and the packaging
         decision is E8.S6's; the obligation is stated HERE so that neither of those two being
         dropped can ship the engine with no notice.

         The version is PINNED: every figure in benchmark-fournisseurs.md §6.2/§10 and every number
         in the E8.S1 spike was measured against 0.5.1. -->
    <PackageReference Include="BergamotTranslatorSharp" Version="0.5.1" ExcludeAssets="native" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Phrasebook data: embedded in the exe (so a single portable exe is self-contained)
         AND copied next to the exe so it stays easy to edit. -->
    <None Remove="Data\phrases.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Data\phrases.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </EmbeddedResource>
    <None Remove="Data\slang.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Data\slang.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </EmbeddedResource>
    <None Remove="Data\squad.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Data\squad.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
